788  OPTHOSONAL POLYNOMIALS
22.17. Orthogonal Polynomials of a Discrete Variable
In this section some polynomials f_n(x) are listed which are orthogonal with respect to the scalar product
22.17.1  (f_n, f_m)=\sum\limits_{i}w^*(x_l)f_n(x_l)f_m(x_l).
The x_l are the integers in the interval a\leq x_l\leq b and w^*(x_l) is a positive function such that
